   "design": "The ultrasound machine takes patient and order data from the radiology worklist ({OTHER}), so images carry the right patient and exam without typing. A rule set proposes the procedure code from the order and exam type, and the sonographer confirms it. Procedure documentation uses a structured template per exam type. Once the sonographer has checked the record, the exam closes and goes to billing.",
   "previous_blocker": "Patient details were typed on the machine and codes looked up by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Modality worklists and rule-based code proposals are standard in radiology systems.",
   "still_hard": "Combined or unplanned procedures do not match the rule set.",
   "human_edge": "Noticing an image labelled with the wrong side before it reaches the radiologist.",
